{"id": "CAP-023-04", "type": "tooling_opportunity_candidate", "title": "Type-build failures can emit source siblings and change source test resolution", "content": "An early tsc -b without a newly required composite reference emitted JS/declaration siblings outside GAT rootDir into dependency src directories. Vite then resolved JS and bypassed TS source aliases, causing misleading missing-built-entry errors. Record missing-reference diagnostics, remove only verified untracked generated siblings, and restage corrected project references before repeating builds. Consider preventing out-of-root emit or noEmitOnError in verification tooling.", "status": "captured", "discovered_at": "2026-10-04", "candidate_kind": "aiws_system_improvement", "suggested_target": "tooling", "improvement_scope": "project", "reusable": true, "source_refs": ["verification/prerequisite-types-01.log"]}
{"id": "CAP-023-05", "type": "insight", "title": "Independent Agent scheduling needs an explicit root tool context", "content": "Actual built SDK replay exposed ambient tool-parent propagation into a separately scheduled child Agent. Host withAgentDriver validates the exact live generation, leaves the tool context only while scheduling, restores the caller context, and keeps ordinary nested parent/capability checks. Replay must assert the actual child reply reaches parent history before accepting refreshed expectations.", "status": "captured", "discovered_at": "2026-10-04", "candidate_kind": "reusable_pattern", "suggested_target": "wiki_reference", "improvement_scope": "project", "reusable": true, "source_refs": ["sdk-qualification.md", "docs/gat-design/DETAIL_DESIGN.md"]}
{"id": "CAP-023-06", "type": "tooling_opportunity_candidate", "title": "Generated references need explicit replacement ownership", "content": "Installing GAT alongside retained prototype packages creates duplicate service/event declarations in exhaustive catalog generators. Exclude only explicitly paired prototype paths when entry projects both exclude the prototype and reference a valid nonempty replacement; retain exhaustive visibility elsewhere and fail on incomplete declarations.", "status": "captured", "discovered_at": "2026-10-04", "candidate_kind": "aiws_system_improvement", "suggested_target": "tooling", "improvement_scope": "project", "reusable": true, "source_refs": ["verification/catalog-discovery-final.log", "docs/gat-design/DETAIL_DESIGN.md"]}
{"id": "CAP-023-07", "type": "wiki_meta_update_candidate", "title": "Registered GAT design changed during prerequisite implementation", "content": "Formal prerequisite delta and source mappings changed registered architecture/basic/detail/integration/map documents. Intended capture is a source-meta refresh request; installed tooling names this kind wiki_quality_issue rather than the playbook wiki_source_refresh_needed. Prepare reviewed metadata from final hashes; existing metadata remains historical until HUMAN-controlled promotion. Never infer current implementation from stale AIP-EXEC-022 hashes.", "status": "captured", "discovered_at": "2026-10-04", "candidate_kind": "wiki_quality_issue", "suggested_target": "wiki_meta", "step": "STEP-06", "improvement_scope": "project", "reusable": true, "source_refs": ["docs/gat-design/DETAIL_DESIGN.md", "docs/gat-design/source-code-map.json"]}
